    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This is a unique opportunity to rent a property on Ireland's southernmost inhabited island.\r\n\r\nAtlantic View on Cape Clear Island, County Cork is the historic former home of the Cadogan seafaring family and is uniquely situated overlooking the picturesque South Harbour.\r\n\r\nIt has been fully renovated throughout and is now a comfortable three bedroom, two bathroom house.  There is a new fitted kitchen, modern shower room upstairs and a lovely snug living room with a solid fuel stove.   The floors are wood or tiled.\r\n\r\nThis property is available for long term rental and potentially could also provide an opportunity for farming / growing on the adjacent 50 acres of land.  This would be an additional separate agreement if it were suitable.\r\n\r\nCape Clear is renowned for dramatic cliff views, birdwatching, and marine life and the property is accessed via ferry from Baltimore Harbour.\r\n\r\nThe local primary school is a safe and scenic 20 minute walk from the house which makes it ideal for a family with younger children.\r\n\r\nHeating is from the fireplaces and electric heaters.  Hot water is electric also.  Water is from the island water scheme.\r\n\r\nRental / s are essential.  Price on application.\r\n\r\nAccommodation;\r\n\r\nKitchen / Dining / Living Room with solid fuel stove, snug sitting room with solid fuel stove, rear hall with utility area, bathroom with bath, wc. and hot press,  sun room (suitable for office / playroom space)\r\n\r\n1st Floor;  Three bedrooms and one shower room"
      },
